Add conditional `#if CAIRO_HAS_VULKAN_SURFACE`. Good.

Instance creation once under mutex. Need ensure Vulkan surface feature may be built but runtime unavailable. We create device lazily on first surface. If fails, cache failure, return NULL. Global device refcount.

But Vulkan device may be lost. Handle errors as surface status DEVICE_ERROR.

Command submission and synchronization:
- per surface `VkCommandPool`, `VkCommandBuffer`, `VkFence`, descriptor pool/set.
- Buffers: pixel buffer; edge buffer; path buffer; cliprect buffer; params buffer. Each buffer host-visible+coherent, persistent map? For edges/params we write each operation. Map/unmap each time or persistent map. Persistent map: keep pointers. Pixel buffer pointer exposed to image surface. All buffers host visible. Simplify: allocate all `HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT`, map upon creation, keep `void*`.
- Buffer memory type selection: query physical device memory properties, find memory type index with required flags and `!DEVICE_LOCAL` preference. Most host-visible. Use `HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT`.
- Bind descriptor set with 5 buffers and update before dispatch (or whenever buffer handle changes). If buffers recreated, descriptor update.
- Since params buffer needs changing each op, persistent.

Need fence wait, reset fence, command buffer reset/begin, bind pipeline/descriptor, dispatch, pipeline barrier for SSBO writes? Within one dispatch, no need. Memory barrier after compute to host? Use fence; but for host read visibility, need `vkCmdPipelineBarrier` COMPUTE->HOST? Spec: fence wait makes memory writes available, but host reading needs `VK_ACCESS_HOST_READ_BIT` dependency. Could add barrier at end: srcStage COMPUTE, dstStage HOST, srcAccess SHADER_WRITE, dstAccess HOST_READ. Then fence. Good.
